meta {
  name: 21 Bulk Action (Collect All)
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/bulk/collect
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{sampleId}}"],
    "tubeType": "EDTA (Purple)",
    "notes": "Bulk collected from the selection toolbar",
    "skipInvalid": false
  }
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
  test("returns an array of updated samples", function () {
    if (res.getStatus() < 400) expect(res.getBody().data).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  Representative **bulk** action (§A.11). Every single-sample action has a bulk
  twin at `POST /accession/order-samples/bulk/<action>` taking `{ "ids": [...] }` **plus
  the same action fields**, applying the transition to all ids in one transaction
  (up to 500). Available bulk actions: `collect`, `collect-print`, `accept`,
  `acquire`, `halt`, `error`, `hold`, `repeat`, `store`, `discard`, `return`,
  `cancel`, `retrieve`, `assign-barcode`.

  ## `bulk/assign-barcode` (group barcode)

  `POST /accession/order-samples/bulk/assign-barcode` with `{ "ids": [...] }` and
  an optional `"barcode"` assigns **one shared barcode** to every id (the FE sends
  a whole group's `sampleIds`). Omit `barcode` to allocate the next
  system-sequential value (from `10001`); a single Code 39 image is rendered and
  its S3 URL stored in `orderIdBarcode` on all members, in one transaction.

  ## `skipInvalid` (group actions — "send all + skip invalid")

  Optional boolean (default `false`). When `false` the batch is strict: if any id
  is not in a legal state for the action the whole request fails with 422
  `INVALID_SAMPLE_TRANSITION`. When `true` (used by the grouped in-house page's
  Order / Department / Department+Sample action buttons, which send every
  `sampleIds` in the group) samples not in a legal state are **skipped** and the
  response returns only the ids that transitioned.

  ## `force` (group status actions — "direct status override")

  Optional boolean (default `false`). When `true`, the action is applied to
  **every** id **regardless of its current status** — the transition legality
  check is skipped and each sample is set to the action's fixed target status
  (Accept→ACCEPTED, Halt→HALT, Acquire→ACQUIRED, …). Used by the grouped in-house
  page's status buttons so e.g. Accept on a group of mixed New/Collected/Accepted/
  Halted samples sets them **all** to ACCEPTED. `retrieve` is never forced.
}
